  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full set at Webster Hall on December 1, 2009, capturing a night that fans later described as absolutely amazing [3][2]. The recommended recording, uploaded by nyctaper, is a matrix mix of soundboard and audience microphones that documents the entire 99-minute performance [1]. This setlist includes the first archived appearance of “Genesis 3:23” and the mythic rarity of “Hebrews 11:14,” which has only two archived performances [1]. Listeners of the separate audience recording by bluesmer noted the surprise of hearing “Song for Dana Plato” live, a track with only six archived performances [4][2]. The show also featured “Against Pollution,” a bustout that had not appeared in 53 previous archived shows [1]. The band closed with a four-song encore, including “Ezekiel 7 and the Permanent Efficacy of Grace” and “Going to Georgia” [1]. This performance is the 148th in the archive’s collection for the band, following their November 28 show at the Theatre of the Living Arts [6]. Visual documentation of the event includes photos taken by Thomas Hartnett [8][9]. A poster for the tour, credited to bumpershine, promoted the Webster Hall date alongside a documentary screening [7]. The nyctaper recording is preferred for its complete 22-song lineup and documented lineage [1].",
